\title{Paloor Language Resources for K-12 Curriculum Development}
\author{Compiled by Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5) for Andr\'as Kornai}
\date{}
\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{Introduction}
Paloor (ISO 639-3 \texttt{fap}; also Palor, Falor, Palar) is a Cangin language of the Atlantic-Congo family spoken in the Thi\`es region of Senegal. The Palor are ethnically Serer but do not speak Serer. Sources give speaker numbers between 5,000 and about 14,500. It is closest to Ndut. No school use was found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school materials were found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, ``Palor language''. The main scholarly source it points to is Paula d'Alton's 1987 grammatical and phonological sketch with lexicon and texts (not itself located online). \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palor_language}
\item Wikipedia, ``Cangin languages''. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cangin_languages}
\item Montebran, slides/paper on Cangin languages (22. Afrikanistentag, Berlin, 2016). \url{https://www.iaaw.hu-berlin.de/de/region/afrika/aktuell/archiv/22-afrikanistentag-juni-2016/montebran_berlin-cangin-2.pdf}
\item Endangered Languages Project bibliography for Paloor. \url{https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/7711/bibliography?hl=de}
\item Verbix endangered languages entry for Paloor. \url{https://docs.verbix.com/EndangeredLanguages/Paloor}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project profile (listed as Jola, Falor) in Senegal; mission-oriented demographic profile. \url{https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/people_groups/11185}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
No audio, video, corpus or software resources were found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Paloor is a small, apparently stable community language with only scholarly descriptions available. A curriculum would require new materials, an agreed orthography, and coordination with the Senegalese national language framework, which this search did not examine.
\end{document}
